{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1459,
    "dDurationMs": 4031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are plenty of objects that are good\nat blocking light and casting shadows; clouds,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5490,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trees, birds, tables, people, the moon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8460,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what about light itself?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10580,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can photons cast shadows?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13030,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At first glance, the answer appears to be\nno."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15840,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light - photons - are electromagnetic waves,\nand electromagnetic waves don’t directly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20980,
    "dDurationMs": 1199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interact with themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22179,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Other waves in nature - waves in shallow water,\nfor example - can directly bounce off of or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26529,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least influence each other . But not photons\n- they just pass right through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31089,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s why sunlight doesn’t block cell\nphone signals, or human vision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35629,
    "dDurationMs": 4741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, there are three indirect ways that\nphotons CAN interact with other photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40370,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, if a photon bumps into, say, an electron,\nand that electron bumps into another photon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45440,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the photons will technically have redirected\neach other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47980,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this requires an electron to be in just\nthe right place at the right time, so I don’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52260,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think this really counts as a way for a photon\nby itself to make a shadow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56020,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, just like how photons passing close\nto massive objects like the sun or a black"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hole follow paths curved by gravity, a photon\nitself has energy and momentum and would technically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gravitationally deflect another passing photon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the gravity from a photon is ridiculously\ntiny - even the most energetic photon we’ve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73640,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ever measured had a smaller gravitational\nfield than a strand of (virus) DNA . Which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77869,
    "dDurationMs": 2601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "won’t allow a photon to make a noticeable\nshadow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80470,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, third and finally, super high energy\nphotons can spontaneously turn into particle-antiparticle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86390,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pairs (like an electron and positron), and\nthen back again - and these particles can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90740,
    "dDurationMs": 3781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "deflect or absorb other photons, resulting\nin legit photon-on-photon scattering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94521,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I say “legit” because the key here is\nthat you don’t need to luck out and have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98540,
    "dDurationMs": 4969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an electron happen to be passing by - two\nsolitary (if high-energy) photons can spontaneously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103509,
    "dDurationMs": 3811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "generate their own means of crashing into\nor bouncing off each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107320,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what kind of shadow do we get?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109060,
    "dDurationMs": 5059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, photons only bounce off each other exceedingly\nrarely Even very very carefully controlled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114119,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experiments with ridiculously high powered\nlasers have a hard time observing any interaction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118479,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119859,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which doesn’t sound promising for noticing\na shadow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122409,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, there is one very real way that photons\ncast shadows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126409,
    "dDurationMs": 4541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because space is so huge, super high energy\nphotons traveling through it DO eventually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130950,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crash into one of the many (low energy) photons\nof the cosmic microwave background radiation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135500,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are present pretty much everywhere in\nthe universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138010,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, right now, you are literally being\nshadowed from ultra high energy gamma ray"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141970,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "photons by the photons left over from the\nbig bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146780,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s sponsor time!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148990,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which means Particle Fever promotion time!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151350,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I’ve recommended it before because it’s\nan amazing documentary about particle physics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154660,
    "dDurationMs": 3081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I’m gonna recommend it again because\nI know not all of you have watched it on Curiosity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157741,
    "dDurationMs": 3279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stream yet - otherwise why would they still\nbe sponsoring MinutePhysics videos?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161020,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, in addition to Particle Fever, Curiosity\nStream has a deal going on right now - if"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164940,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get a curiosity stream subscription (which\ncosts less than a cup of coffee), you now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168840,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also get a bundled subscription to Nebula,\nthe streaming service made by and for educational"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173820,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "youtube video creators, with ad-free viewing\nand exclusive originals, like Real Engineering’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178500,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "series on the insane logistics of D-Day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181260,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So go to curiositystream.com/minutephysics\n(and use offer code minutephysics) to get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your first month of curiosity stream and nebula\nfor free."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188600,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just think how many times you can watch Particle\nFever in a month!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
